---
source: tests/help_pages.rs
description: "a command's -h and --help pages as this build renders them at 100 columns without color; any change to an about, a flag, a value, a heading or the layout changes them: review with cargo insta review, or re-accept with INSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test --test integration help_pages:: and review git diff tests/snapshots/"
---
==> omaddons robot-docs install-skill -h <==
Install the agent guide as a skill (SKILL.md) where coding agents load skills

Usage: omaddons robot-docs install-skill [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --dir <DIR>
          The skill folder to write SKILL.md into (default: $HOME/.claude/skills/omaddons; created
          if its parent exists)

Global options:
      --json
          One JSON envelope on stdout

      --robot
          The same as --json

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format
          
          [possible values: json, human]

  -t, --target <TARGET>
          The client to act on: id, key, game mode (sod and hardcore select the Classic Era client),
          family, product, flavor folder, path, or all (every client)
          
          [alias: --flavor]

      --dry-run
          Show the plan without changing anything (ignored by commands that change nothing)

      --actor <ACTOR>
          Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]

      --reason <TEXT>
          Why, recorded verbatim in history (at most 200 characters; ignored by commands that change
          nothing)

      --offline
          Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]

      --while-running
          Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)

      --if-match <TOKEN>
          Change nothing unless the plan is still the one the --dry-run that returned this token
          (data.precondition) showed

      --no-color
          No ANSI color

      --no-progress
          No progress output

      --progress <MODE>
          Progress events on stderr
          
          [possible values: json, human, none]

      --quiet
          Only errors on stderr

  -v, --verbose...
          More detail (repeatable)

  -h, --help
          Show help

Examples:
  omaddons robot-docs install-skill              for Claude Code
  omaddons robot-docs install-skill --dry-run    what it would write
  omaddons robot-docs install-skill --dir $HOME/.codex/skills/omaddons

Writes the agent guide, the same bytes as omaddons robot-docs guide, as SKILL.md in
the skill folder. The default needs $HOME/.claude and creates skills/omaddons in it; a
--dir folder is created when its parent exists. A SKILL.md you edited is kept as
SKILL.md.bak. It never writes through a symlink, into a game client, a Wine prefix or
omaddons' own folders. omaddons doctor reports an installed skill that holds another
guide than this build's. Remove the skill by deleting the folder.
